# L §3.2, §8.4: the kind spending keeps transfers' leg cash of unit any, so load can't show the unit of the sum of
# o.cash.amount; it is checked at the key.  q: 100.00 PLN x 0.5 rounded to minor(PLN) = 50.00 PLN (L §7.2).  q2: the sum
# there is 30.00 EUR x 0.5, whose unit really differs from the step minor(PLN): RUN-DOMAIN at that key.  (Was refused
# at load: LOAD-UNIT round: the step money PLN and dyn have different units.)
=== m.tally
model p8
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "synthetic"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
unit EUR: currency minor 0.01

kind spending: transfers
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place konto_e: accounts EUR lives 2025-01-01..
place shop_e: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input bank: observed
input share: num
input win: month

def spent: money PLN
  rule base = round(sum(o.cash.amount for o in bank over win where o in spending and o.cash.from == konto) * share, minor(PLN), half-up) when covered(konto, win)

def spent_e: money PLN
  rule base = round(sum(o.cash.amount for o in bank over win where o in spending and o.cash.from == konto_e) * share, minor(PLN), half-up) when covered(konto_e, win)

version st
  cite s
  governs 2026-01
  known 2026-02-02
  covers konto, konto_e
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-01-05, kind: spending, leg cash from konto to shop amount 100.00 PLN)
  bank[r2] = (on: 2026-01-06, kind: spending, leg cash from konto_e to shop_e amount 30.00 EUR)

version facts
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  share = 0.5
  win = 2026-01
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  opening[konto_e] = 100.00 EUR at 2026-01-01 start "s"

ask q: spent
ask q2: spent_e
=== expect
q: 50.00 PLN
  cut 2026-10-18
q2: refused: RUN-DOMAIN round: the step 0.01 PLN and 15.00 EUR have different units
  cut 2026-10-18
